WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.520
Build a triangle.

2
00:00:01.570 --> 00:00:06.350
Each row starts and ends with one, and
every other entry is the sum of the two

3
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:07.360
above.

4
00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:09.460
Now take powers of eleven.

5
00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:12.170
Eleven squared is one two one.

6
00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:15.070
Eleven cubed, one three three one.

7
00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:18.960
And eleven to the power four
is one four six four one.

8
00:00:19.010 --> 00:00:20.690
The digits are the rows!

9
00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:21.780
Coincidence?

10
00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:24.090
Does every power of eleven do it?

11
00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:27.310
In this mission, you'll
meet the binomial theorem:

12
00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:33.050
row n of Pascal's triangle gives the
coefficients of a plus b to the power n.

13
00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:38.280
You'll find each entry as n choose
r, by formula or on your GDC.

14
00:00:38.330 --> 00:00:43.170
Your mission: explain why the digits of
eleven to the power four form a row of

15
00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:44.590
Pascal's triangle.
